<!--
  The dock: Meta Notes' home, and the only screen at launch. Floating glass
  buttons with nothing between them but passthrough: Settings, Templates,
  Recent in one line, and New note, the main action, at the right end
  (where the dominant hand finds it; mirrored for left-handed use later).
  Settings opens a panel with preferences (stick mode, on by default) and
  account connections (Google Drive, Microsoft); Recent a grid of up to
  six notes (ink, title and when it was edited), with a Recents / Show all
  toggle for a scrolling grid of every note (filtered by when it was
  edited and its paper, sorted by date or title); Templates a grid of six
  papers with a line on what each is for. While a panel is open the
  buttons fade away and it takes their place, centred where the eye
  already is; its close button (or picking an item) brings them back. The
  thin bar underneath is the grab handle for moving the dock.

  First launch (no notes): #dock-hint, one short line above the buttons,
  points at New note; it goes once the first note exists.

  The round buttons, the pop-up and the hint have no background here: the
  dock system puts a liquid-glass slab behind each (src/ui/liquid-glass.ts).
  New note is the theme's primary action, clay with white ink. Element ids
  are addressed from src/systems/compact-dock-system.ts; keep them stable.
-->
<style>
  @font-face {
    font-family: ui;
    src: url(../fonts/bricolage-text.ttf);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: ui;
    src: url(../fonts/bricolage-ui.ttf);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .dock {
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .dock-row {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .dock-button {
    width: 56px;
    height: 56px;
    border-radius: 28px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    color: #f7f2ea;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .dock-new {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
